Data
----

Each data directory names its sources, licences, changes and attributions in
its own LICENSES.md:

backend/imtihan/tasks/LICENSES.md
  ARC-AGI-2 tasks (ARC Prize Foundation, Apache License 2.0), TruthfulQA
  questions (Lin, Hilton and Evans, Apache License 2.0), XSTest prompts
  (Röttger et al., CC BY 4.0). Everything else there was written for MIZAN.

backend/tadbir/data/amanah/LICENSES.md
  Windows of deepset/prompt-injections and jackhhao/jailbreak-classification
  (Apache License 2.0), Lakera/gandalf_ignore_instructions,
  reshabhs/SPML_Chatbot_Prompt_Injection and microsoft/llmail-inject-challenge
  (MIT), FineWeb-Edu (ODC-By 1.0, also subject to the Common Crawl terms of
  use), Tatoeba (CC BY 2.0 FR), and lines written for MIZAN (CC0 1.0).

backend/tadbir/data/lughah/LICENSES.md
  Tatoeba sentences (CC BY 2.0 FR), Hinglish-Everyday-Conversations-1M (MIT),
  every seventh ayah of the Quran's Uthmani text from the Tanzil Project
  (verbatim, under Tanzil's terms: LICENSES/LicenseRef-Tanzil.txt), and lines
  written for MIZAN (CC0 1.0).

backend/tadbir/data/qamus/LICENSES.md
  Word lexicons computed from MASSIVE 1.1 (Copyright Amazon.com Inc. or its
  affiliates, CC BY 4.0) and, for Roman Hindi/Urdu, Aksharantar (AI4Bharat,
  IIT Madras; CC BY 4.0 and CC0 1.0). No utterance of either is included.

backend/tadbir/data/gharib/LICENSES.md
  words.json.gz is adapted from wordfreq's data (Robyn Speer, 2022,
  https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.7199437) and is licensed under CC BY-SA 4.0
  (LICENSES/CC-BY-SA-4.0.txt), with the sources wordfreq asks to credit.

backend/tadbir/ruh_reader/LICENSES.md
  The sources the Ruh reader is trained and measured on. Its corpus and
  weights are downloaded and built on the machine that trains it, not shipped.

backend/research/datasets/LICENSES.md
  The research package's inputs: the Amiri font (above) and tags written for
  MIZAN are shipped; the Quranic Arabic Corpus morphology (Kais Dukes, GPL,
  https://corpus.quran.com), Quran.com's word-by-word glosses and the hadith
  collections are downloaded from their sources when the scripts run.

backend/tadbir/data/qasd/facets.tsv
  Lines written for MIZAN (CC0 1.0) and requests from MASSIVE 1.1 train
  (Copyright Amazon.com Inc. or its affiliates, CC BY 4.0).

backend/tadbir/data/iqtibas/calibration.tsv
  Short quotations of the Quran's text from the Tanzil Project (Tanzil's
  terms), its transliteration, and the Saheeh International translation, to
  calibrate one parameter.

ruh_model/benchmarks/data/morph_gold_qac_test.tsv
  172 (word, root) pairs from the test split of Q-CSMP v2 (CC BY 4.0). Its
  roots follow the annotation of the Quranic Arabic Corpus
  (https://corpus.quran.com).


Downloaded when MIZAN runs
--------------------------

MIZAN downloads some data and models once, from their original sources and
pinned by SHA-256 where the source allows, into $MIZAN_DATA_DIR: among them
the Quranic Arabic Corpus morphology (GPL), the hadith collections of
fawazahmed0/hadith-api, the Quran editions Fihris reads, the NLI model and the
Whisper weights. They are not part of this repository and keep their own
licences; docs/architecture.md lists the external services and data.
